#: source/release-notes/rl-0.9.md:1
msgid "Release 0.9 (2005-09-16)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.9.md:3
msgid ""
"NOTE: this version of Nix uses Berkeley DB 4.3 instead of 4.2. The database "
"is upgraded automatically, but you should be careful not to use old versions "
"of Nix that still use Berkeley DB 4.2. In particular, if you use a Nix "
"installed through Nix, you should run"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.9.md:10
msgid "first."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.9.md:12
msgid ""
"Unpacking of patch sequences is much faster now since we no longer do "
"redundant unpacking and repacking of intermediate paths."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.9.md:15
msgid "Nix now uses Berkeley DB 4.3."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.9.md:17
msgid ""
"The `derivation` primitive is lazier. Attributes of dependent derivations "
"can mutually refer to each other (as long as there are no data dependencies "
"on the `outPath` and `drvPath` attributes computed by `derivation`)."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.9.md:22
msgid ""
"For example, the expression `derivation         attrs` now evaluates to "
"(essentially)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.9.md:25
msgid ""
"    attrs // {\n"
"      type = \"derivation\";\n"
"      outPath = derivation! attrs;\n"
"      drvPath = derivation! attrs;\n"
"    }\n"
"    "
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.9.md:31
msgid ""
"where `derivation!` is a primop that does the actual derivation "
"instantiation (i.e., it does what `derivation` used to do). The advantage is "
"that it allows commands such as `nix-env -qa` and `nix-env -i` to be much "
"faster since they no longer need to instantiate all derivations, just the "
"`name` attribute."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.9.md:37
msgid ""
"Also, it allows derivations to cyclically reference each other, for example,"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.9.md:40
msgid ""
"    webServer = derivation {\n"
"      ...\n"
"      hostName = \"svn.cs.uu.nl\";\n"
"      services = [svnService];\n"
"    };\n"
"     \n"
"    svnService = derivation {\n"
"      ...\n"
"      hostName = webServer.hostName;\n"
"    };\n"
"    "
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.9.md:51
msgid "Previously, this would yield a black hole (infinite recursion)."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.9.md:53
msgid ""
"`nix-build` now defaults to using `./default.nix` if no Nix expression is "
"specified."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.9.md:56
msgid ""
"`nix-instantiate`, when applied to a Nix expression that evaluates to a "
"function, will call the function automatically if all its arguments have "
"defaults."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.9.md:60
msgid ""
"Nix now uses libtool to build dynamic libraries. This reduces the size of "
"executables."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.9.md:63
msgid ""
"A new list concatenation operator `++`. For example, `[1 2 3] ++ [4 "
"5         6]` evaluates to `[1 2 3 4 5         6]`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.9.md:68
msgid ""
"Some currently undocumented primops to support low-level build management "
"using Nix (i.e., using Nix as a Make replacement). See the commit messages "
"for `r3578` and `r3580`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.9.md:72
msgid "Various bug fixes and performance improvements."
msgstr ""
